--TEST--
A child `Core\Process::spawn` started is stopped when the program ends, and one still running that the program never waited for or killed is an error on standard error that fails the run — `rule:core-classes/process-spawn`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Process::spawn
// The child reads its input to the end, and the program holds that input open,
// so it is still running when the last statement returns. Nothing catches the
// error: the program has already ended, so it is reported the way an uncaught
// throw is, after everything the program printed, and the run exits with 1.

string $path = "/bin/cat";
if (Core\Env::OS == Core\Env::Platform::Windows) {
    $path = "C:\\Windows\\System32\\sort.exe";
}
Core\Process\Handle $child = Core\Process::spawn($path, []);
echo "started\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.process]
exec = true
--EXPECT--
started
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
{"level":"error","msg":"A process started with `Core\\Process::spawn` was still running when the program ended, so it was stopped. Call `wait()` or `kill()` on its handle before the program ends.","fields":{"program":"%s"}}
